  "limitations": [
    "Synthetic constant-score loopback fixtures on shared hardware with 20 ms artificial delay per HTTP request; no live-provider relevance, token billing or universal speed claim.",
    "Linux is the authorized ARM64 Docker VM, not an independent native Linux host.",
    "Concurrency can increase peak RSS. CPU and first-output medians are reported alongside elapsed time; fewer requests do not imply every metric improves.",
    "Child wait4 RSS includes runtime/startup/file mappings, not only heap allocations. First stdout is emitted after ranking completes in ranked cases; the streaming case explicitly disables ranking.",
    "Warm scores still require current authorization, revision and image-byte validation. Server-owned asset identities and complete cross-write predicate certificates remain separate contracts.",
    "The source registry contains only ephemeral scalar facts. It does not retain bodies, ACL decisions or predicate answers, and is never persisted or restored across owners.",
    "Raw reports/logs remain ignored local artifacts; their checksums are recorded but they are not published downloadable evidence.",
    "One prior macOS full run entered conservative wide-directory watcher fallback; the same case failed on the old binary and passed isolated on the current binary. The final full native suite passed.",
    "Windows is cross-compiled only; Windows runtime and real providers are not qualified."
  ],
